# Kontrakt Noncommercial Source License 1.0

**Version 1.0 — official public license text**

This is a **source-available**, not an OSI-approved open-source, license. It is an operative public license for the copyright-protected Kontrakt material to which its authorized rightsholder applies it, as specified in Section 1. It offers free permission only within the noncommercial scope below. Commercial permissions require a separate authorization. The English text is controlling.

## 1. Scope and definitions

1.1 **Licensor** means each copyright holder or other rightsholder that publishes or has authorized publication of its rights in the official Kontrakt project under this License. Each Licensor grants only rights it owns or is legally authorized to grant. The official Kontrakt project is the upstream distribution published or expressly endorsed by the relevant rightsholder, not an unaffiliated fork. **Recipient** is a person or entity exercising rights under this License. The public identity and provenance of a Licensor may be evidenced by the applicable original copyright notices, upstream repository publication records, and contribution-rights records; no separate release notice is required to activate this License.

1.2 **Covered Software** means the original Kontrakt source code and corresponding object code which an authorized rightsholder distributes in an official repository revision or release containing this License, except files or portions expressly identified as governed solely by another license. This License applies to the extent the corresponding rightsholder has authority to grant it, and does not withdraw any earlier license. A recipient may determine the applicable revision or release from its provenance, repository commit, tag, distribution archive, and accompanying license files. Previously granted permissions for earlier Apache-licensed copies remain unaffected. **Covered Modification** means a modified or combined work containing copyright-protected expression from Covered Software, including adaptations of that expression. The presence of a Covered Modification does not make separately authored, legally independent portions of the work Licensor-owned. **Contributor Addition** means original code supplied by a person other than Licensor and included in a Covered Modification; its ownership and licenses are determined by Sections 3.3 and 3.4 unless separately assigned to Licensor. Implementing an idea, published specification, protocol, algorithm, functionality, or compatible interface independently, without copying protected expression, does not by itself create a Covered Modification.

1.3 **Commercial Activity** means an activity in which a person or entity reproduces, installs, executes, modifies, builds, distributes, or otherwise exercises rights in Covered Software or a Covered Modification **as part of that person's or another identifiable person's business or paid professional workflow**. This includes business-directed research, procurement evaluation, prototypes, development, compilation, testing, verification, optimization, CI/CD, maintenance, deployment, and operation of internal systems, products, services, or contractual deliverables. An activity performed by an employee or contractor for a business remains Commercial Activity when performed on a personal device, personal account, or external infrastructure. Selling access to Covered Software, paid hosting or compilation, and distribution materially conditioned on payment or a paid subscription are also Commercial Activity. The activity need not produce revenue, profit, a released product, or a measurable performance improvement. **A third party's later or incidental business benefit, without a separate covered-code act by or for that third party, does not reclassify an earlier lawful noncommercial activity.** A person does not incur a commercial-license duty merely by publishing independently authored software that another entity later uses.

1.4 **Permitted Noncommercial Activity** means an activity involving Covered Software that is not Commercial Activity and consists of (a) an individual's learning, hobbies, experimentation, independent research, noncommercial development, or voluntary community contributions; or (b) education, independent academic research, public research, or other noncommercial public-interest activity by a Qualifying Organization, performed for its own educational, scientific, or public-interest mission. Salaries, tuition, academic grants, scholarships, cost reimbursement, publication of results, and sponsorship do not **by themselves** make the activity commercial. The exception does not cover using Covered Software to perform a contractual deliverable for an identifiable commercial customer, to develop or validate that customer's proprietary product or operational system, or to provide that customer's contracted engineering, compilation, verification, or maintenance service. Contractual control of the deliverable, customer acceptance obligations, confidential customer-specific specifications, or exclusive operational handover may evidence that relationship; **funding source or a possible later commercial application alone is not conclusive**. Publicly disseminated research under an ordinary unrestricted research grant is not made commercial merely because companies may use its findings.

1.5 **Qualifying Organization** means an educational institution, public research institution, or nonprofit/public-interest organization **only for the particular activity** satisfying Section 1.4(b). Organizational status alone does not qualify its business contracts, procurement work for a commercial customer, or independently operated commercial services. **Authorized Recipient** means an individual acting within Section 1.4(a) or a Qualifying Organization acting within Section 1.4(b).

1.6 **Commercial Authorization** means a separate, express authorization executed by Licensor for a specifically identified recipient and scope, whether paid or explicitly granted without charge. **Named Authorization** means a Commercial Authorization issued at no charge or a reduced charge to an identified person or entity; it does not arise by status, reputation, size, funding, or implication.

## 2. Noncommercial copyright grant

2.1 **Only for Permitted Noncommercial Activity**, and subject to Sections 3–5, Licensor grants each Authorized Recipient a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free copyright license, continuing unless terminated under Section 8, to reproduce, install, execute, study, modify, and create Covered Modifications of the Covered Software, and to distribute Covered Software or Covered Modifications under Section 3. The license covers the Recipient's lawful acts, not acts performed on behalf of a separate commercial beneficiary.

2.2 A Qualifying Organization may authorize its personnel, students, volunteers, and research collaborators to carry out the organization's Permitted Noncommercial Activity. Such persons do not thereby receive authorization for unrelated clients, employers, subsidiaries, sponsors, or their own Commercial Activity.

2.3 The grant does not authorize Commercial Activity. Any enterprise carrying out activities under Section 1.3 must obtain Commercial Authorization for the relevant covered-code acts, including internal research, test environments, CI/CD, and production operations. The business need not distribute a product or demonstrate a direct financial return. Employees, independent contractors, consultants, and intermediaries may not substitute their personal eligibility for the authorization required by an identifiable commercial principal. Nothing in this Section creates a legal presumption that shifts a statutory burden of proof.

2.4 Browsing public source, discussing ideas, publishing independent implementations, and exercising statutory rights do not require permission under this License to the extent they do not implicate rights controlled by Licensor. Merely publishing or submitting an upstream patch is not by itself a sale or sublicense of Covered Software; commercial build and deployment activities still require their own authorization.

## 3. Modifications, forks, and noncommercial distribution

3.1 Authorized Recipients may create, keep private, publish, and distribute noncommercial forks and Covered Modifications. Each distribution must: (a) retain the applicable copyright, license and attribution notices; (b) supply this License with the original terms; (c) identify significant modifications; (d) make the corresponding source code for the distributed Covered Software and Covered Modifications available at no charge in a reasonably accessible form; and (e) distinguish unofficial forks from official Kontrakt releases.

3.2 The source obligation applies to the Covered Software and protected modifications actually distributed, including scripts reasonably necessary to build those portions. It does not impose a license on separately owned, independently developed programs merely aggregated or interoperating with them. Recipients must also respect third-party licenses.

3.3 A distributor who owns or controls rights in a Contributor Addition contained in a Covered Modification distributed under this Section grants each downstream Authorized Recipient a direct, worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free, non-sublicensable copyright permission for that addition solely for the same Permitted Noncommercial Activity, source-provision, notice, and redistribution conditions. The distributor also grants a limited patent permission **only for claims it has authority to license that are necessarily infringed by that addition as supplied and exercised within those permitted activities**. No patent permission is implied for unrelated combinations, modifications made by others, or business use. If the distributor cannot grant rights necessary to distribute the addition in that way, it must obtain permission or exclude the addition. Ownership of independently authored additions remains with their owner unless separately assigned.

3.4 An eligible recipient of a fork receives permission for Licensor-owned portions directly from Licensor under Section 2, and receives permission for Contributor Additions from their respective owners under Section 3.3 or another independently valid grant. An enterprise using the fork in Commercial Activity must obtain Licensor's Commercial Authorization **and separately obtain any rights required for Contributor Additions**. A fork author cannot sell, sublicense, expand, or replace Licensor's commercial authorization; nor does Licensor purport to grant commercial rights in third-party additions it does not control.

3.5 Renaming, rebranding, partial rewriting, refactoring, translation, obfuscation, relocation to another repository, or distribution through an intermediary does not remove restrictions on protected expression that remains copied or adapted from Covered Software. A recipient may not falsely present Licensor-owned portions as permissively or commercially relicensed, or a fork as an official Kontrakt release. **No percentage-of-change threshold is created by this License.** These rules do not claim ownership of independently authored code, create a presumption of copying, or require an independent implementer to prove a clean-room development process merely because an implementation is compatible.

3.6 Distribution or access to Covered Software or a Covered Modification in exchange for a fee, subscription, paywalled release, bundled sale, paid managed deployment, materially contingent sponsorship, or other bargained-for commercial consideration requires Commercial Authorization. Voluntary unconditional donations and ordinary attribution alone do not necessarily make an otherwise Permitted Noncommercial Activity commercial. Independently offered services that do not exercise rights in Covered Software are not automatically prohibited.

## 4. Commercial permission and named exceptions

4.1 Commercial Activity involving acts for which Licensor's permission is legally required needs a Commercial Authorization **before those acts begin**, except to the extent that a statute independently permits the particular act. Internal-only business use, evaluation for business adoption, absence of revenue, and receipt of a public fork do not themselves create commercial permission. No automatically renewable evaluation period is provided by this License; a business may request a scoped written Evaluation Authorization.

4.2 Commercial Authorization may cover specified legal entities, versions, projects, personnel, contractors acting for the authorized entity, build infrastructure, hosted services, and redistribution according to the signed agreement or order form. Permission to operate Kontrakt internally does not itself confer rights to redistribute the compiler, provide it as a service to customers, sublicense it, or include it as a general-purpose developer tool in other products.

4.3 A Named Authorization applies only to its specifically identified recipient, permitted work, term, release scope, and beneficiaries. Affiliates, parents, subsidiaries, customers, acquirers, suppliers, and contractors do not acquire independent rights merely through their relationship with the recipient. Any approved use by contractors solely on the authorized recipient's behalf must be expressly within its stated scope. Transfers, mergers, changes of control, and any subsequent use are governed by the executed authorization and applicable mandatory law; a change in share ownership alone is not presumed to change the identity of the licensee.

4.4 A later commercial transition does not retroactively turn completed lawful noncommercial activities into infringements. New acts requiring commercial rights after a change of purpose or beneficiary require authorization. Existing independent outputs remain subject to their own rights and applicable embedded-component licenses.

## 5. Outputs, embedded components, and third-party rights

5.1 Using Kontrakt does not transfer ownership of a user's independent source code, Contracts, Realizations, data, or independently authored output to Licensor. Mere compilation does not make every resulting application a Covered Modification or automatically impose a royalty on its downstream purchasers.

5.2 Copyright-protected Kontrakt-owned runtime code, helpers, templates, or libraries **actually included in or distributed with an output** remain subject to the license lawfully applicable to those components. A release that embeds such protected components in generated outputs must identify the components and the terms on which they may be redistributed, including applicable downstream rights, in an accompanying component notice or manifest. The absence of such a notice does not enlarge any right in actually copied protected code, and does not turn independently authored output into Covered Software. No obligation arises merely from an undocumented or hypothetical inclusion. A distributor must verify the rights applicable to any protected components it actually redistributes.

5.3 A customer purchasing only an independently authored application does not require Kontrakt compiler authorization solely because the application was built with Kontrakt. An operator actually running Kontrakt for another person's development, compilation, verification, or build service performs its own licensable acts and may require separate commercial service authorization.

5.4 Earlier versions validly distributed under Apache License 2.0 or other licenses retain the permissions previously granted for those versions. Third-party components remain under their own licenses. No provision purports to relicense unrelated code without its owner's authority.

## 6. Limited patent license

6.1 **Necessary Claims** means patent claims that the relevant Licensor **owns or has enforceable authority to license** and that are necessarily infringed by exercising the express permissions for the relevant Covered Software version as supplied by that Licensor. Necessary Claims do not include patents owned by other parties that have not been assigned or expressly sublicensed to Licensor, or claims infringed only by third-party modifications, unrelated combinations, or independent implementations. For a contribution incorporated into an official release, the applicable copyright and patent authority must be verified through the project's contribution-rights process **before acceptance**. A contributor's public submission or GitHub fork alone does not automatically transfer patent ownership to Licensor.

6.2 Subject to the conditions of this License, each relevant Licensor grants Authorized Recipients a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free patent license under Necessary Claims solely as necessary to exercise the copyright permissions in Sections 2 and 3. A Commercial Authorization must expressly identify or incorporate the patent rights available for its scope; no commercial patent permission or coverage of unowned third-party claims is implied by this Community grant. For unmerged third-party forks, any limited patent grant by the fork author is governed by Section 3.3, not by Licensor's grant under this Section.

6.3 To the extent legally permitted, the patent license granted to a Recipient under Section 6.2 terminates if that Recipient initiates a patent proceeding alleging that **Licensor-supplied Covered Software, or an unchanged Licensor-supplied portion as present in a Covered Modification, infringes** a patent claim controlled by that Recipient. The alleged infringement must concern the supplied code or its expressly permitted exercise, not a feature caused solely by a third party's independent addition or combination. A defensive response to a prior patent action over Covered Software does not itself trigger this termination. This Section does not terminate unrelated copyrights, rights granted by other owners, or any right whose termination is prohibited by law.

## 7. Notices, trademark, and source identity

7.1 Applicable copyright notices, the original licensing identification, and material modification notices must be preserved where the corresponding work is distributed. No Kontrakt trademark or official certification license is granted. Accurate attribution and lawful statements of compatibility are unaffected.

7.2 Official release notices, verified hashes and signed release artifacts may identify the applicable release and its licensing terms; their absence or presence does not itself create an evidentiary presumption or reverse a legal burden of proof.

7.3 Commercial copying or extraction of Covered Software for training, fine-tuning, or assembling software models requires the applicable copyright permission unless the particular activity is independently permitted by law. Noncommercial coding assistants used within permitted activities, nonwaivable research exceptions, and independently authored implementations remain outside this prohibition to the extent protected by law. A separate machine-readable rights reservation may be published where a statute requires it; this statement alone is not represented as satisfying every legal formality.

## 8. Compliance and termination

8.1 Acts outside the grants above are not authorized **by this License**. Whether a particular act is copyright infringement, breach of a separately formed contract, or permitted by mandatory law depends on the applicable law and facts. No automatic damages multiplier or universal infringement presumption is imposed.

8.2 A first inadvertent failure by an otherwise eligible noncommercial distributor to supply source or notices may be corrected within 30 days after written notice identifying the defect. Timely complete correction preserves or reinstates rights to the extent legally permitted. This correction opportunity does not grant an organization 30 days of free commercial use or retroactively authorize an unlicensed business activity.

8.3 Subject to any mandatory legal cure rights, a material failure to comply terminates the permissions concerned. Properly licensed downstream recipients do not automatically lose their independent grants because an upstream distributor defaults. Prior valid releases and independently authored outputs keep their independent legal status.

## 9. Statutory rights and international application

9.1 This License offers uniform, worldwide public copyright and limited patent permissions. It does **not** claim that a single national law can govern the existence, scope, infringement, exceptions, and remedies of intellectual-property rights worldwide. Those matters are governed by applicable territorial and conflict-of-laws rules. In the absence of a separately agreed and valid choice of law, contractual questions are determined under the applicable conflict-of-laws rules. This clause is not a waiver of enforcement or of otherwise available judicial remedies.

9.2 Nothing restricts rights that cannot lawfully be waived, including applicable lawful observation, testing, interoperability, backup, error correction, exceptions and limitations, exhaustion, and protected independent creation. Each party may seek relief before a court having jurisdiction under applicable law; this public License neither establishes a worldwide exclusive forum nor imposes compulsory arbitration on Community Recipients. The separate Commercial Agreement must state its chosen law and forum or arbitration mechanism. Any unenforceable provision is severed only to the minimum extent permitted without expanding Licensor's grant or defeating mandatory user protections.

## 10. Disclaimer and final provisions

10.1 To the maximum extent permitted by law, Covered Software is provided **AS IS**, without warranties of merchantability, fitness, availability, support, title, or noninfringement. Licensor's liability is excluded or limited only to the extent law permits. Paid agreements may provide separate warranties, indemnities, support and remedies.

10.2 This License does not authorize covert telemetry, collection of recipients' proprietary source code, or undeclared remote disablement. The terms of a separate commercial agreement, and any valid affirmative acceptance to that agreement, determine additional contractual duties; a public repository visit does not by itself establish a signed commercial contract.

10.3 A Licensor may offer rights it controls under other licenses without modifying existing grants. No FAQ, README, unilateral website change, unofficial fork, or distributor's notice changes the grant already applicable to an identified revision or release. The binding public terms are this fixed English text as included by the authorized rightsholder in the corresponding official distribution, subject to the applicable component and prior-license notices. New versions of this License apply only when expressly adopted for the corresponding material; they do not retroactively change an earlier grant.

